## Development Workflow (TDD)

```
Spec → TDD Test (RED) → Implement (GREEN) → Verify → Report → Commit
```

- Specs use OpenSpec format at `openspec/changes/{feature-name}/`
- Write failing tests BEFORE production code
- Commit footer includes `Spec:` + `Scenarios:` + `AI-assisted: yes`

## Pre-commit Verification (Stage 7.5)

Before any commit, you MUST:

1. Run the relevant test suite — must be green.
2. Cross-check implementation against `openspec/changes/{name}/specs/{name}/spec.md`
   line-by-line — 0 CRITICAL findings required.
3. Generate / update `openspec/changes/{name}/report.md` summarizing coverage.

If any of the above fails, fix before committing. Do NOT bypass this gate.

## PR Comment Fix Workflow (Stage 11)

When fixing a PR review comment:

- Address ONE comment per commit. No batching.
- First produce a fix PLAN (files, changes, spec mapping, risks, confidence) —
  do NOT edit yet. Wait for human approval.
- After plan approval, apply the minimal change — no drive-by refactoring, no
  unrelated cleanup.
- If the comment contradicts the spec, surface the conflict; do not silently
  override the reviewer.
- Commit footer for PR-comment fixes:

  ```
  fix(review): {scope} address {file}:{line} - {summary}

  Comment: {reviewer_name} on {file}:{line}
  PR: #{PR_ID}
  Spec: openspec/changes/{name}/specs/{name}/spec.md
  Scenarios: {scenario-name}
  AI-assisted: codex
  ```

- Do NOT push. Do NOT mark the discussion as resolved — the human verifies
  the diff first, then the pipeline resolves it.

## Branching And Worktree

- New specs MUST work in a fresh worktree at `.worktrees/{name}` on
  `feat/{branch_name}`. Do not work in the main repo for new specs.
- Never push directly to protected branches ({integration_branch}, `main`).
- Never use `git push --force` or `--force-with-lease` without explicit user
  approval.
